  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 81,
  "sortOrder": 19081,
  "verseCount": 16,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Sing aloud unto God our strength: make a joyful noise unto the God of Jacob.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Take a psalm, and bring hither the timbrel, the pleasant harp with the psaltery.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Blow up the trumpet in the new moon, in the time appointed, on our solemn feast day.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For this was a statute for Israel, and a law of the God of Jacob.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "This he ordained in Joseph for a testimony, when he went out through the land of Egypt: where I heard a language that I understood not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "I removed his shoulder from the burden: his hands were delivered from the pots.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Thou calledst in trouble, and I delivered thee; I answered thee in the secret place of thunder: I proved thee at the waters of Meribah. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Hear, O my people, and I will testify unto thee: O Israel, if thou wilt hearken unto me;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "There shall no strange god be in thee; neither shalt thou worship any strange god.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "I am the LORD thy God, which brought thee out of the land of Egypt: open thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "But my people would not hearken to my voice; and Israel would none of me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "So I gave them up unto their own hearts’ lust: and they walked in their own counsels.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Oh that my people had hearkened unto me, and Israel had walked in my ways!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "I should soon have subdued their enemies, and turned my hand against their adversaries.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "The haters of the LORD should have submitted themselves unto him: but their time should have endured for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:81:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "He should have fed them also with the finest of the wheat: and with honey out of the rock should I have satisfied thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 81:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:81:16"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
